    "description": "Class III, mains-operated, self-indicating, price-computing, single or dual-interval, non-automatic weighing instruments designed for direct sales to the public. Construction: plastic housing, operator's keypad, stainless steel load receptor, operator front touch screen display, customer rear LCD display, level indicator, integrated printer. Devices: initial zero setting device (up to 20% of Max), semi-automatic zero setting device (up to 4% of Max), zero tracking device (up to 4% of Max), automatic zero setting device (up to 4% of Max), zero indicator, net indicator, stable weight indicator, semi-automatic subtractive tare balancing device, preset tare, gravity compensation, price computing, totalisation (including non-weighed items), PLU, fixed weight labelling, multi-vendor operation, calibration/set-up mode via sealed internal switch, self-service operation, modular display (with fixed legally relevant areas), self-service operation (CL7200-S). Interfaces: RS232C, cash drawer, Ethernet, wireless LAN, USB. Software designated V3.xx.x, displayed at power up; software download only possible via the USB interface and protected by switches on the sealed main board. Sealing: access to the load cell, electronics, calibration and software download switches prevented by wire seal or tamper-evident label."
